Tasks/NSC-007.yaml:70:      "requirement": "Solid gameplay colliders block Fireball's projectile: walls, obstacle and prop colliders (shelves, pews, columns, rubble), and any door whose doorway-blocker collider is enabled (sealed, locked, and broken doors, since a broken door keeps its one-way player blocker by design); only an open door the wizard has not yet crossed does not block. FireballProjectile tests this each Tick with a chest-height Physics.Raycast (or equivalent sweep) against non-trigger colliders, using the same default-layer, trigger-ignoring query the ranged enemy caster's HasUnobstructedViewOfWizard already uses (EnemyFireballCaster on main; NSC-077 renames it EnemyLanternWispCaster, and either name satisfies this), and ignoring colliders on the wizard's own CharacterController; no new layer, tag, collider, or query API is introduced. Fireball never collides with or damages the caster. Enemies carry no colliders, so contact is a flat horizontal distance test against active, non-defeated EnemyHealth objects within the projectile's configured contact radius, matching DemoRunFlow's existing enemy-contact pattern; this contract does not add enemy colliders. On contact with an enemy or a blocking collider, the projectile detonates: it damages the contacted enemy and, for tiers above tap, every other active, non-defeated enemy within that tier's configured area radius that has an unobstructed line (the same raycast rule) from the detonation point, damaging each enemy at most once per cast. Nothing behind a wall or a closed door is damaged. Damage goes only through EnemyHealth.TakeDamage(float).",
