Tasks/NSC-077.yaml:51:      "requirement": "Put the approved enemy art on the enemies that DoorPrototypeGlobalSceneBuilder.BuildChaseEnemies already builds into Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, in place of their generated placeholder silhouettes. Every MeleeEnemy (NavMeshAgent, EnemyTargetKnowledge, EnemyPursuitMovement, EnemyHealth) uses the Melee Enemy (Dungeon Brute) art. Every ranged enemy, today a FireCasterEnemy with EnemyFireballCaster and EnemyHealth, becomes a Lantern Wraith (AC-007) and uses the Ranged Enemy (Lantern Wraith) art. Keep the Enemies root, spawn positions, counts, components and all gameplay tuning. Do not add prefabs, review-only enemies or room placements; the stationary review prefabs and review placement of contract revision 2 are dropped."
Tasks/NSC-077.yaml:81:      "requirement": "Turn the scene's fire caster into the Lantern Wraith without changing its gameplay. The builder names each ranged enemy GameObject LanternWraith instead of FireCasterEnemy. EnemyFireballCaster becomes EnemyLanternWispCaster: move EnemyFireballCaster.cs to EnemyLanternWispCaster.cs together with its tracked .meta in the same commit, so EnemyLanternWispCaster.cs.meta keeps the script GUID 73b9fddab19c3f34e878119acd894458 (Docs/Engineering/UNITY_TESTING_POLICY.md: Unity assets move with their .meta files, and a tracked .meta is never deleted or regenerated as a relocation mechanism). A model-write-scoped execution crew cannot rename .meta files, so this move is a host-owned git move of both files made by the integrating session; a pipeline-generated replacement .meta with a new GUID does not satisfy this criterion. Keep its public Initialize, Tick, CurrentMana and IsOutOfMana members, its serialized field names and every serialized default (60 mana, 10 mana per cast, 1 second cast interval, 14 unit cast range, projectile speed 8, hit radius 0.8, lifetime 4 seconds, 5 damage). Its projectile GameObject is named LanternWisp and shows a glowing teal ghost-light orb, unlit or emissive in the art bible's teal #30e0cb, with no fire colors, at today's projectile size. The wraith's placeholder asset key becomes LanternWraithSprite, the unused FireCasterEnemySprite.asset and its .meta are deleted, and no fire naming or fire colors remain in the wraith's builder code, script or projectile. The legacy FireCasterEnemy entry in DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder's clear list stays, because that file is not edited. The wisp orb is a stand-in: Vincent picked the look on 2026-09-16 (the \"grumpy face\" sample A wisp, a lantern-flare wind-up and a ring-pop hit), and that art replaces the orb in a later task once its production pass is committed (INT-002)."
Tasks/NSC-077.yaml:103:      "requirement": "EnemyArtIntegrationTests opens the saved Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity without saving and proves that every MeleeEnemy and LanternWraith under the Enemies root, with at least one of each and no FireCasterEnemy, has one Animator using its enemy type's controller, one EnemyAnimationController, a Visual SpriteRenderer showing its south idle still instead of a placeholder, the NSC-039 world-sprite sorting, a uniform Visual scale of 1 and the camera-facing Visual rotation, with EnemyAnimationController's camera-rotation constant equal to DoorPrototypeGlobalSceneBuilder.IsometricCameraEulerAngles, and the gameplay components and NavMeshAgent settings the builder gave that enemy before this task, with EnemyLanternWispCaster in place of EnemyFireballCaster."
Tasks/NSC-077.yaml:113:      "requirement": "EnemyLanternWispCasterPlayModeTests drives EnemyLanternWispCaster.Tick against a wizard with PlayerHealth and proves the gameplay EnemyFireballCaster had at b05a06ee1: it casts at once when the wizard is within 14 units with a clear view and not when the wizard is out of range or behind a wall collider; it casts once per second, spending 10 of its 60 mana per cast, so it stops after six casts; projectiles travel 8 units per second for at most 4 seconds and deal 5 damage through PlayerHealth.TakeDamage within 0.8 units. Every projectile is a GameObject named LanternWisp that renders the teal ghost-light color with no fire color. The test also covers the additive read-only range and view members used by AC-006."
Tasks/NSC-077.yaml:123:      "requirement": "On the exact candidate, with Unity closed on that checkout: run DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.Build twice and require that the second run changes no file's bytes except Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity. That binary scene is re-saved with regenerated local fileIDs on every build, so for it require semantic identity with the first run's output instead: the same object count per class and per MonoBehaviour script GUID, and the same sorted serialized object sizes per class and script GUID; record that comparison as delivery evidence. Require a clean compile; pass EnemyArtIntegrationTests, EnemyAnimationPlayModeTests and EnemyLanternWispCasterPlayModeTests; pass the existing EnemyPursuitPlayModeTests, EnemyPursuitDoorCrossingPlayModeTests, EnemyTargetKnowledgePlayModeTests, EnemyHealthPlayModeTests, ActiveEnemyRegistryPlayModeTests, EnemyLockedDoorAttackPlayModeTests, DoorEnemyPassabilityPlayModeTests, WizardAnimationPlayModeTests, WizardArtIntegrationTests and DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests fixtures, using the semicolon-separated Edit Mode and Play Mode test filters recorded for NSC-077 in Pipeline/TaskReviewAgent/authoritative_validation_policy.json. Two DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests tests went stale before this task, when commit 9a3d22c56 (the playable build) moved the player to PlayerSpawnPosition: Build_PlayerStartsAtCharacterControllerGroundedHeight and Build_MainCamera_FramesPlayerAndStartingDoorInView. They do not block this task when they also fail with the same assertion on the candidate's base commit; record the base and candidate results for both. Every other test in both filters must pass; confirm that the diff under Art/Enemies/Source changes only .png.meta files and that the saved scene has no missing-script references after the rename, that EnemyLanternWispCaster.cs.meta keeps GUID 73b9fddab19c3f34e878119acd894458, and that neither EnemyFireballCaster.cs nor EnemyFireballCaster.cs.meta remains; and commit only builder output plus the files this task registers."
Tasks/NSC-077.yaml:164:  "notes": "Revision 3 replaces revision 2's stationary, presentation-only review scope at Vincent's direction on 2026-09-16: \"So 77 needs to be changed. We have moving enemies. We need to integrate the art into the already created enemies that have no art.\" It absorbs NSC-094's walk animation scope; NSC-094 is superseded by this task. The same day Vincent decided the ranged enemy becomes the Lantern Wraith and its fireball becomes a teal ghost-light lantern wisp with the same gameplay (art-director guide section 11, item 2). The reconciliation key keeps its original stationary wording because reconciliation keys never change. On main the scene enemies come from the playable-build commit 9a3d22c56, which has no task: MeleeEnemy moves through NSC-092's EnemyPursuitMovement and NSC-091's EnemyTargetKnowledge, and the fire caster holds its ground with EnemyFireballCaster and no NavMeshAgent, which no test covers. Their code is integrated on main; missing delivery records for NSC-075, NSC-091 and NSC-092 are graph bookkeeping, not missing code. RangedEnemyKeepDistanceMovement (NSC-053), RangedEnemyAttack and RangedEnemyProjectile (NSC-054) are not used by the scene's ranged enemy and are outside this task; their Lantern Wraith wording belongs to the NSC-016 and NSC-055 revisions. The Melee Enemy north-east single-cleaver idle and walk correction, approved by Vincent, is on main since b05a06ee1. walk_00 to walk_05 are PixelLab frames 1 to 6; the start pose was never committed. Revision 4 (2026-09-16) applies Vincent's pixel-density decision B: characters are a 128x128 canvas at about 64 pixels per unit in a camera-facing 2x2-unit box. The enemy art is already drawn at 128, so only the import constant and the Visual box change; the wizard's re-make and its own camera-facing Visual are separate work. The Art Director advised the pivot rules and the VAL-008 checks. Attack, hit and defeat animations need new approved art and a separate task. The unmerged branch codex/nsc077-stationary-enemies-20260914 may be read for its source-inventory check only; do not merge or copy its prefabs, review placement, copied PNGs or scene, and never delete it. Lessons: GUID-only stub .meta files import as Cube with point-light cookie defaults in Unity 6000.1 (NSC-075 fixes 0d28b0bf5 and bf97d116c), so set the texture shape and reset the cookie defaults explicitly; DoorPrototype.unity is binary, so rebuild it with the builder and never merge scene files; NSC-075 shipped with its screen-up axis inverted and its tests encoded the same mistake until Vincent saw it in Unity, which is why AC-005 spells out the mapping and VAL-008 requires his in-game check; Unity test filters are separated by semicolons. No .asmdef, ProjectSettings, DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs or WizardAnimationController.cs change is authorized; stop and report if one is needed.",
